# question: Can coinciding alarms be identified whom together form a different clinical meaning than their independent meaning, and for which no individual alarm exists?
#
# NOT an answer to CQ11 -- see ../cq_discoveries.md's CQ11 entry: the
# framework has no vocabulary or inference mechanism for an emergent,
# combined-alarm concept, so no query can actually answer this CQ. This is
# a DIAGNOSTIC query instead, illustrating the gap the same way the
# manuscript's Box 3 does: for any snapshot where more than one distinct
# PhysiologicalProcess is reachable from the alarms active at that instant,
# report both the alarms and the processes. The absence of a third,
# combined concept in the result IS the finding -- there is nothing here
# to derive one from, structurally, regardless of what pattern the query
# looks for.
#
# Deliberately does NOT try to attribute a specific alarm instance to a
# specific process via a direct property path (e.g. alarm ->
# hasMessage/triggeredBy/...) -- that edge is a STATIC archetype-blueprint
# relation (kg_generated.ttl) and is never asserted on a grounded alarm
# instance in the operational/temporal layer (confirmed empirically: zero
# mda:triggeredBy triples exist on any alarm instance in this graph). An
# alarm instance and the metric/process facts revealed alongside it are
# only ever co-present in the same snapshot, never linked by a direct RDF
# path -- the same constraint CQ9/CQ10 were built around from the start.
#
# reasoning: required (same graph-shape notes as CQ9/CQ10: snap:forPatient
# outside GRAPH ?g; the diagnostic chain's final two hops -- approximates,
# isPropertyOf -- only resolve inside the tick's named graph, since Metric
# is Stateful/condition-scoped)
#
# Validated against the fabricated dataset (DATA/CQ_evaluation/
# events_data.csv): fires on cq11_pos (PHILIPSMONITOR - Lage hartfreq. +
# SERVOU - Ademfrequentie laag -> CardiacContraction, PulmonaryVentilation,
# no third concept) as intended. Also correctly fires on cq10_neg (SpO2 laag
# + HF hoog -> PulmonaryOxygenation, CardiacContraction) -- not cherry-picked
# to only match the one illustrative case; any patient with two coinciding,
# genuinely unrelated processes matches the same way.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX snap: <https://w3id.org/mda/snapshot/>

SELECT ?patient (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?label; separator=" | ") AS ?alarms)
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?process; separator=" | ") AS ?processes) WHERE {
  ?g snap:forPatient ?patient .
  GRAPH ?g {
    ?alarm mda:hasLabel ?label .
    ?analysis mda:producesMetric/mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf ?process .
  }
}
GROUP BY ?patient
HAVING (COUNT(DISTINCT ?process) > 1)
ORDER BY ?patient
